# OPTIONAL O1 (after L3; four cards, separable): the same reading at the contexts L3 leaves out: one fast user beside 2 and 1 standard
# users at 32,768 tokens, and beside 3 at 120,000 tokens (2,048 tokens out), c2-packed-tp4-lanes-time-gate, the ratio swept on each
# boot. The 120k arm is where the modelled frame is longest (P(4) 102 ms and F 59 ms at phase 1 against 85 and 53 at 4k), so it is the
# arm that says how much of the target survives a full-context coding agent.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card lanes window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it
# over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lanes and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image L0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 3-8 min plus 4-12 min of streams (the 120k arm's four serial prefills are
# about 40 s each): 25-60 min for three arms. Step limit 380 min; worst case 186 min. C2_GATE_JIT=record as in L1.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lanes-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=lanes-timing-more
C2_GATE_JIT=record
